    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23253" root="شوأ" body-key="$">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَآءَنِى</span></b> , formed by transposition from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَآنِى</span>,
aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَشُوْءُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَشِىْءُ</span>, [but the latter form of the
aor. is disallowed by MF,] <i>He preceded me,</i> or
<i>outwent me.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <i>He grieved me.</i> (K.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>He pleased me.</i> (K.) Thus it bears two
contr. significations. (TA.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُؤْتُهُ</span>, aor.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشُوْؤُهُ</span>, <i>I pleased him.</i> (Lth, O.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُؤْتُ بِهِ</span> <i>I
was pleased with, and rejoiced in, him,</i> or <i>it.</i>
(Lth, O, K.) [See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شأو</span>.]

